Dependency archive
------------------
mixxx-deps-2.7-arm64-android-1c20f84a.zip, sha256
6786c09f491166352880984842ffa6f554e974f30a3766a2392298444c1be83c, built from
https://github.com/mixxxdj/vcpkg at 1c20f84aa1ffca2ef18a7d9c6bd7cdd1f5f2e265 (triplet
arm64-android). The recipes and sources of every package are in that vcpkg repository and
the upstream projects; each package's licence text is its copyright file in the archive
under installed/arm64-android/share/<package>/copyright. The build scripts replace two
parts of your extracted copy (the zip is never modified):
  - lib/libportaudio.a is rebuilt from PortAudio b0cc303e with the Mixxx overlay patches
    0001-0004 and our repair 0005 (tools/android-preview/portaudio/);
  - FFmpeg is rebuilt from the same vcpkg commit without the Fraunhofer FDK AAC library and
    with FFmpeg's own LGPL AAC decoder (tools/android-preview/03b_ffmpeg_no_fdk.sh).

Fraunhofer FDK AAC is excluded: the APK contains no FDK AAC code. The archive's FFmpeg is
built with it, so it is removed before linking; Qt Multimedia's prebuilt FFmpeg plugin (which
also embeds it) is not bundled. Consequence: Mixxx's optional AAC/HE-AAC recording and
broadcasting encoder, which loads a user-supplied libfdk-aac, is unavailable on Android.

