Separate shared libraries in the APK (lib/arm64-v8a/):
- Qt 6.10.3 (Core, Gui, Network, Sql, Widgets, Xml, Concurrent, OpenGL, PrintSupport, Test,
  Core5Compat, Qml, Quick, Quick Controls 2, Quick Layouts, Quick Shapes, Quick Dialogs,
  Quick Effects, Svg, SvgWidgets, ShaderTools, Multimedia, plus their QML plugins and the
  platform, style, TLS, image-format, icon-engine, SQL-driver and Android media plugins):
  LGPL-3.0 (alternatively GPL-2.0-or-later or GPL-3.0, depending on the module), used here
  under the LGPL-3.0. They are the unmodified builds from the dependency archive, loaded as
  shared libraries, so you can replace them with your own build of the same Qt version (the
  Qt source is at https://download.qt.io; the exact recipe is mixxxdj/vcpkg above). Qt's SQL
  driver plugin for PostgreSQL contains libpq 18.3 (PostgreSQL Licence) and Qt's TLS plugin
  and that driver contain OpenSSL 3.6.2 (Apache-2.0).

Not in the APK although the dependency archive has them: Fraunhofer FDK AAC, the Qt FFmpeg
media plugin, the QML debugger and profiler plugins (qmltooling), PortMidi, and the other
packages of the archive that Mixxx does not link on Android (for example Ableton Link, bit7z,
7zip, benchmark, gtest, Qt tools and Designer).

Fonts: the OpenSans fonts (Apache-2.0) and Ubuntu fonts (Ubuntu Font Licence) in res/fonts keep their own licence files.
